## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  redactionVersion: string;
  implicatedRegions: string[];
  tenantIds: string[];
  severity: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the effectiveness of the redaction rollback in production?
- Which metrics would you surface to product and compliance teams during a breach incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CAPA program around data privacy, tenant isolation, and controlled policy changes in real-time fintech systems.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners, policy references
- Tenant-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify with SLAs
- Minimal API: create/update CAPAs with logs/traces, policy links
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, tenant impact
- RCA and canary rollback: structured **root cause** templates and safe rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch: POST /api/capa
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {evidence, lineage, owners, policyLink, tenantId} = req.body;
  // validate inputs, create CAPA, emit logs, assign owners
  res.status(201).json({capaId: 'CAPA-1234'});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in evidence and logs metadata?
- What would be your go/no-go criteria for canary rollback validation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of drift in a multi-tenant streaming system with region isolation, ensuring containment without collateral impact. It also probes data lineage, governance, and rollout discipline.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with tenant scope, region, evidence, ownership, and lineage
- Region-tenant gated lifecycle to prevent cross-tenant bleed
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked logs/traces
- Tenant-scoped metrics: containment MTTR, drift score, recurrence rate, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollback plan for sessionization logic changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: CAPA data model (conceptual)
class CAPA {
  constructor(id, tenantId, region) {
    this.id = id;
    this.tenantId = tenantId;
    this.region = region;
    this.evidence = [];
    this.rootCause = null;
    this.actions = [];
    this.owner = null;
    this.state = 'DETECTED';
    this.timestamps = {};
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test isolation between tenants during a canary rollout?
- How would you handle cross-tenant drift if tenants share resources?

